kind: fix
upstream: not yet reported to V-HACD (which its author considers deprecated).

Voxelizing welds vertices at 1/1000 of the mesh's scale and drops the
triangles that collapse, then divides by the extent of what is left: when
nothing is left that is 0 / 0, and the NaN is cast to size_t, which is
undefined. Treat it like the existing no-points case: an empty volume.

Reproduced 2026-11-01 with clang -fsanitize=undefined: a tetrahedron 1e-7
across plus one unused vertex at (1, 1, 1), which sets the mesh's scale:
  pristine:  VHACD.h:5119:53: runtime error: -nan is outside the range of
             representable values of type 'unsigned long'
  patched:   clean, 0 hulls
Covered by: tests/test_vhacd.py::test_everything_welded_away (that input,
run under UBSan by `uv run scripts asan`), fuzz/vhacd.cpp.

--- a/include/VHACD.h
+++ b/include/VHACD.h
@@ -5108,6 +5108,12 @@
     m_bounds = BoundsAABB(points);
 
     VHACD::Vect3 d = m_bounds.GetSize();
+    // trimkit (vendor/patches/vhacd-empty-volume.patch): nothing left after welding
+    // dropped every collapsed triangle is an empty volume, not 0 / 0 cast to size_t
+    if (!(d.MaxCoeff() > 0.0))
+    {
+        return;
+    }
     double r;
     // Equal comparison is important here to avoid taking the last branch when d[0] == d[1] with d[2] being the smallest
     // dimension. That would lead to dimensions in i and j to be a lot bigger than expected and make the amount of
